From 592a27a5a0376a80db2271c6e97c4f7643b279d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:06:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 38/71] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: add sound card support for eliza

Add an eliza_priv_data entry and a "qcom,eliza-sndcard" compatible
match so the SC8280XP machine driver drives the audio card on the
Retroid Pocket Duo (eliza).

The board has an AW88166 speaker amp on Primary MI2S and an ES8326
headset codec on Quaternary MI2S, with the LPASS as bit-clock and
frame master on both links:

  - mi2s_mclk_enable / mi2s_bclk_enable: the SoC drives MCLK and BCLK
    on the MI2S links.
  - codec_dai_fmt = BC_FC | NB_NF | I2S: the codecs run as I2S clock
    consumers. This is inert for the AW88166 (no .set_fmt) and tolerated.
  - codec_sysclk_set: propagate the MCLK rate to the codec with
    snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk(). The ES8326 needs it to pick its
    clock-divider coefficients; without it the codec logs "Clock
    coefficients do not match" and leaves its dividers unprogrammed.
    The AW88166 has no .set_sysclk op and tolerates -ENOTSUPP.
  - wcd_jack: register the headset jack used by the ES8326 jack detect.

Signed-off-by: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index 4d48e1012..f1b4b8b3f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -443,6 +443,12 @@ static const struct qcom_snd_soc_common eliza_priv_data = {
 	.dapm_widgets = sc8280xp_dapm_widgets,
 	.num_dapm_widgets = ARRAY_SIZE(sc8280xp_dapm_widgets),
 	.wcd_jack = true,
+	.mi2s_mclk_enable = true,
+	.mi2s_bclk_enable = true,
+	.codec_sysclk_set = true,
+	.codec_dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BC_FC |
+			 SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_NF |
+			 SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S,
 };
 
 static const struct qcom_snd_soc_common hawi_priv_data = {
